The desk merged reports about wrong dates into #4471. The live breakdown groups unique reports by tenant locale and booking form, rather than by the intake tag.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What to investigate

- **Shared parser:** The parser reads month first even for tenants who write day first. Check date interpretation across channels.
- **Booking-v3 hint:** The form displays a month-first hint but reads the input in the tenant's day-first order. Make the hint and interpretation agree.

The table also flags reports that the desk read as a one-day move but filed by tenant under a cause. Review those reports individually; a month/day swap does not by itself explain a one-day difference.

The subject-only duplicate rule can merge different causes and split matching causes across tickets. Read the reports and tenant details when triaging; the accepted decision record remains unchanged.

